pretty simple challenge but i struggled with finding the proper packets to look for in wireshark when i started 

so with a little help online i managed to find how to filter out the required packets 

since we are looking for TFTP packets i filtered the packets for tftp but then there were still more packets so i added another filter 

tftp.type this gave me only the required files 

then i exported all the contents in the packet by selecting them 

file -> export -> tftp 

once extracted we are provided with a few files 

namely instructions.txt, plan.txt both of these files contained encryted data 


i copied the data from instructions and decrypted it using dcode.fr and it was a ROT13 encryption 

this was the output 

TFTPDOESNTENCRYPTOURTRAFFICSOWEMUSTDISGUISEOURFLAGTRANSFER.FIGUREOUTAWAYTOHIDETHEFLAGANDIWILLCHECKBACKFORTHEPLAN

so i open the plan.txt and again it was encrypted using the same algo 

so i used dcode to solve it and this was the output 

IUSEDTHEPROGRAMANDHIDITWITH-DUEDILIGENCE.CHECKOUTTHEPHOTOS

